# Vue Development Conventions

## Code Style

- Component: use single-file components (SFC)
- API: use the Composition API with the `<script setup>` syntax sugar
- Syntax: use TS for development unless otherwise specified `<script setup lang="ts">`

## Naming

- Component naming: always use PascalCase and avoid conflicts with HTML elements
- Component naming example: refer to the global `SearchMenu` components `@@/components/SearchMenu/index.vue` and `@@/components/SearchMenu/Modal.vue`; note that `index` does not need to follow PascalCase
- Page naming: always use kebab-case
- Page naming example: refer to the CRUD example page `@/pages/demo/element-plus/index.vue`
- Composable naming: always use camelCase
- Composable naming example: refer to the watermark composable `@@/composables/useWatermark.ts`
- Props naming: when declaring a prop, always use camelCase; in templates and JSX always use kebab-case
- Props naming example: when declaring `const { isActive = false } = defineProps<Props>()` and when passing `<Demo :is-active="true" />`
- TS or JS file naming: always use kebab-case
- TS or JS file naming example: `@@/constants/app-key.ts`

## API

- Prefer `ref` over `reactive` when defining reactive variables
- Complex template expressions should be refactored into computed properties or methods
- Avoid circular triggering of watchers to prevent infinite loops

## Props

- Prop definitions should be as detailed as possible, including type, required, and default value
- If TS is used, use type-based declarations, and use reactive props destructuring for default values, e.g. `const { isActive = false } = defineProps<Props>()`

## Routing

- Corresponding directory: `@/router`
- Route names must stay consistent with component names
- The route guard logic is meticulous; do not modify it unless necessary

## State Management

- Corresponding directory: `@/pinia`
- Divide Stores by module
- Prefer Setup Store syntax over Option Store syntax
- Avoid using global state management mindlessly

## Styles

- Prefer Scoped CSS, e.g. `<style scoped lang="scss">`
- Avoid using `!important` whenever possible
- If multiple themes are involved, consider using CSS variables, e.g. `@@/assets/styles/variables.css`

## Other

- Avoid directly manipulating the DOM
- Write atomic components as much as possible
- Always provide a unique `key` when using `v-for` (do not casually use the array index as `key`)
- Do not use `v-if` and `v-for` on the same element at the same time

